  "_comment": "Era I look per region (world area, Act II: Corvane gets its own world). palette = the 4 inks of the screen filter, darkest to lightest; each must stay in its luminance band (<0.25, <0.5, <0.75, >=0.75) so EraManager's filter maps every sprite the same way. The region's tiles are art/era1/tiles/overworld_<region>.png (TilesetFactory.atlas_path; Corvane's from tools/art/gen_tiles_corvane.py, which reads this palette). biome = the look's name, props = what its atlas draws. Regions not listed use the base Ink palette. Post-game regions add their era: Halcyra (era 4, data/region4.json) keeps four inks for the Era I Retro filter, and its Era IV colours are swatches (4 tones each, darkest to lightest) with tiles = TilesetFactory.Kind -> swatch for tools/art/gen_tiles_halcyra.py, which paints art/era4/tiles/overworld_halcyra.png with 8 tones per swatch; stage = colours over data/era4_stage.json for battles in the region (EraManager.stage_colors). Quillmarch (era 3, data/region3.json) has no screen filter: its palette is the 16-colour atlas palette for tools/art/gen_tiles_quillmarch.py (art/era3/tiles/overworld_quillmarch.png); EraManager.inks_for() only takes a four-ink palette.",
